**Complete solution and essential rubric:** Use $D=\sum_r\Delta I_r v_r$ with cases times EUR/case and one consistent price year. Czech narrow counts only Czech receptors at Czech weights: $8(1200)(0.82)=7872.000000$ EUR. Czech broad counts all 24 modelled cases at the same Czech value: $24(1200)(0.82)=23616.000000$ EUR. EU-policy-maker coverage in this checked case includes affected non-EU receptors and uses uniform EU values: $24(1200)=28800.000000$ EUR. Independent observer counts all modelled receptors with their country-specific weights: $[8(0.82)+12(1.1)+4(0.6)](1200)=26592.000000$ EUR. Narrow versus broad changes receptor inclusion with values fixed; broad versus EU changes values with coverage fixed. All-modelled does not mean every global effect is measured, and GDP-based weights are appraisal conventions, not intrinsic human worth. WTP and medical/lost-earnings costs can overlap; add only genuinely separate losses, not automatically a second copy. Historical plant bars are external damages at their configuration/location and stated 2008 price base, not current private tariffs. Danish domestic/foreign source shares concern effects at Danish receptors; deaths abroad are another receptor total. The 2030 Nordic rows have different year/boundary/rounding and cannot be substituted for 2021 shares. Mining variants 1–4 change territorial limits (keep; Bílina; Bílina+partialČSA; both), while perspectives change receptor/value rules within a given variant. No universal one-tonne damage price or current ranking follows. All requested calculations, derivations and qualifications are essential; the component map above applies to every full form.

