## Rubric and independence

Required components: unit_consistent_welfare_sum_and_overlap, four_receptor_value_rules, historical_application_and_scenario_boundaries. Each full prompt/key below elicits every component; all are necessary for a pass on every permitted pair. Accept algebraically equivalent expressions and clearly defined opposite cash-flow signs with correct interpretation. A pass requires all requested outputs/reasons, correct units/assumptions and no critical conceptual error. Partial means a missing component or an unresolved isolated arithmetic slip with an otherwise valid method; independent correction is required for a pass. Fail means a critical mechanism/condition is wrong. Unscorable means a response or its help/exposure conditions cannot be established. Unknown help conditions are never independent evidence.

Critical errors: EU-perspective excludes modelled non-EU receptors in this case; narrow/broad value rules confused; WTP and cost components blindly doubled; 2008 plant costs treated as current tariffs.

Acquisition requires two distinct unused unassisted full checks selected from the six exact metadata routes. Every I/D form covers all components; W1, S1, the prerequisite and C1 are forbidden substitutes. A D form used for acquisition cannot later be counted again as delayed success. No teach-generated item may replace a named full check; additional verified explanation/practice is allowed under the unchanged method and may not fabricate evidence. If fewer than two fresh forms remain for acquisition, return a plan_issue for an additional prepared bank.

| Component | I1 | I2 | D1 | D2 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| unit_consistent_welfare_sum_and_overlap | required | required | required | required |
| four_receptor_value_rules | required | required | required | required |
| historical_application_and_scenario_boundaries | required | required | required | required |

## Misconceptions and correction

An observed omitted term/sign is tentative until the learner explains it; compare the reasoning with the critical errors above. Score the original response before providing help. Route a conceptual failure to the relevant included derivation and prerequisite, then use an unused full form.

O015-C1, item_version 1, narrow_correction. **Prompt:** Czech narrow and broad use the same Czech unit values. Why can their totals differ for the same emission scenario? **Key/rubric:** Narrow includes Czech receptors only; broad includes all modelled receptor populations at those same Czech values. The receptor boundary changes, not the physical emissions or value rule. Pass requires all keyed reasoning; partial for a missing part; fail for the conflicting mechanism. This repairs a common inference only; it cannot substitute for a full numerical/capability check.

Give at most two hints (first identify the date/unit, second point to the included identity); after ineffective hints show the relevant worked step. After two unsuccessful independent attempts stop repeated quizzing, revisit the explanation/prerequisite and preserve the unresolved status.

## Immediate and delayed checks

### O015-I1

O015-I1, item_version 1, full_capability_check. **Prompt:** A hypothetical damage scenario has nonoverlapping additional admission endpoints: Czech receptors 15 cases, other EU receptors 10, and affected non-EU receptors 6; all are in the model’s stated coverage. Uniform EU value is EUR 900/case in a declared common illustrative price year. Relative country-value weights are Czech 0.82, other EU 1.3, non-EU 0.7; these are supplied hypothetical weights, not new empirical country values. Calculate damage under the checked Czech narrow, Czech broad, EU-policy-maker and independent-observer rules. Show the endpoint-unit sum, distinguish receptor boundary from value choice, and explain whether adding a cost-of-illness figure to an already comprehensive WTP value is automatically valid. Interpret why historical 2008 Kč/kWh plant bars, 2021 Danish source shares, 2030 Nordic shares and mining variants 1–4 cannot be collapsed into one current universal damage price.

**Complete solution and essential rubric:** Use $D=\sum_r\Delta I_r v_r$ with cases times EUR/case and one consistent price year. Czech narrow counts only Czech receptors at Czech weights: $15(900)(0.82)=11070.000000$ EUR. Czech broad counts all 31 modelled cases at the same Czech value: $31(900)(0.82)=22878.000000$ EUR. EU-policy-maker coverage in this checked case includes affected non-EU receptors and uses uniform EU values: $31(900)=27900.000000$ EUR. Independent observer counts all modelled receptors with their country-specific weights: $[15(0.82)+10(1.3)+6(0.7)](900)=26550.000000$ EUR. Narrow versus broad changes receptor inclusion with values fixed; broad versus EU changes values with coverage fixed. All-modelled does not mean every global effect is measured, and GDP-based weights are appraisal conventions, not intrinsic human worth. WTP and medical/lost-earnings costs can overlap; add only genuinely separate losses, not automatically a second copy. Historical plant bars are external damages at their configuration/location and stated 2008 price base, not current private tariffs. Danish domestic/foreign source shares concern effects at Danish receptors; deaths abroad are another receptor total. The 2030 Nordic rows have different year/boundary/rounding and cannot be substituted for 2021 shares. Mining variants 1–4 change territorial limits (keep; Bílina; Bílina+partialČSA; both), while perspectives change receptor/value rules within a given variant. No universal one-tonne damage price or current ranking follows. All requested calculations, derivations and qualifications are essential; the component map above applies to every full form.

I1/I2 are immediate checks; D1/D2 are distinct parallel variants reserved where possible for delayed checks. A delayed success requires an unused form before recap, no help/solution access, and at least 24 actual elapsed hours after acquisition and the most recent relevant teaching/solution exposure. Record intervening exposure. A calendar-date change alone is insufficient; an early D attempt is immediate evidence only.

### O015-I2

O015-I2, item_version 1, full_capability_check. **Prompt:** A hypothetical damage scenario has nonoverlapping additional admission endpoints: Czech receptors 12 cases, other EU receptors 18, and affected non-EU receptors 3; all are in the model’s stated coverage. Uniform EU value is EUR 1100/case in a declared common illustrative price year. Relative country-value weights are Czech 0.82, other EU 1.2, non-EU 0.4; these are supplied hypothetical weights, not new empirical country values. Calculate damage under the checked Czech narrow, Czech broad, EU-policy-maker and independent-observer rules. Show the endpoint-unit sum, distinguish receptor boundary from value choice, and explain whether adding a cost-of-illness figure to an already comprehensive WTP value is automatically valid. Interpret why historical 2008 Kč/kWh plant bars, 2021 Danish source shares, 2030 Nordic shares and mining variants 1–4 cannot be collapsed into one current universal damage price.

**Complete solution and essential rubric:** Use $D=\sum_r\Delta I_r v_r$ with cases times EUR/case and one consistent price year. Czech narrow counts only Czech receptors at Czech weights: $12(1100)(0.82)=10824.000000$ EUR. Czech broad counts all 33 modelled cases at the same Czech value: $33(1100)(0.82)=29766.000000$ EUR. EU-policy-maker coverage in this checked case includes affected non-EU receptors and uses uniform EU values: $33(1100)=36300.000000$ EUR. Independent observer counts all modelled receptors with their country-specific weights: $[12(0.82)+18(1.2)+3(0.4)](1100)=35904.000000$ EUR. Narrow versus broad changes receptor inclusion with values fixed; broad versus EU changes values with coverage fixed. All-modelled does not mean every global effect is measured, and GDP-based weights are appraisal conventions, not intrinsic human worth. WTP and medical/lost-earnings costs can overlap; add only genuinely separate losses, not automatically a second copy. Historical plant bars are external damages at their configuration/location and stated 2008 price base, not current private tariffs. Danish domestic/foreign source shares concern effects at Danish receptors; deaths abroad are another receptor total. The 2030 Nordic rows have different year/boundary/rounding and cannot be substituted for 2021 shares. Mining variants 1–4 change territorial limits (keep; Bílina; Bílina+partialČSA; both), while perspectives change receptor/value rules within a given variant. No universal one-tonne damage price or current ranking follows. All requested calculations, derivations and qualifications are essential; the component map above applies to every full form.

### O015-D1

O015-D1, item_version 1, full_capability_check. **Prompt:** A hypothetical damage scenario has nonoverlapping additional admission endpoints: Czech receptors 6 cases, other EU receptors 14, and affected non-EU receptors 8; all are in the model’s stated coverage. Uniform EU value is EUR 1300/case in a declared common illustrative price year. Relative country-value weights are Czech 0.82, other EU 1.4, non-EU 0.5; these are supplied hypothetical weights, not new empirical country values. Calculate damage under the checked Czech narrow, Czech broad, EU-policy-maker and independent-observer rules. Show the endpoint-unit sum, distinguish receptor boundary from value choice, and explain whether adding a cost-of-illness figure to an already comprehensive WTP value is automatically valid. Interpret why historical 2008 Kč/kWh plant bars, 2021 Danish source shares, 2030 Nordic shares and mining variants 1–4 cannot be collapsed into one current universal damage price.

**Complete solution and essential rubric:** Use $D=\sum_r\Delta I_r v_r$ with cases times EUR/case and one consistent price year. Czech narrow counts only Czech receptors at Czech weights: $6(1300)(0.82)=6396.000000$ EUR. Czech broad counts all 28 modelled cases at the same Czech value: $28(1300)(0.82)=29848.000000$ EUR. EU-policy-maker coverage in this checked case includes affected non-EU receptors and uses uniform EU values: $28(1300)=36400.000000$ EUR. Independent observer counts all modelled receptors with their country-specific weights: $[6(0.82)+14(1.4)+8(0.5)](1300)=37076.000000$ EUR. Narrow versus broad changes receptor inclusion with values fixed; broad versus EU changes values with coverage fixed. All-modelled does not mean every global effect is measured, and GDP-based weights are appraisal conventions, not intrinsic human worth. WTP and medical/lost-earnings costs can overlap; add only genuinely separate losses, not automatically a second copy. Historical plant bars are external damages at their configuration/location and stated 2008 price base, not current private tariffs. Danish domestic/foreign source shares concern effects at Danish receptors; deaths abroad are another receptor total. The 2030 Nordic rows have different year/boundary/rounding and cannot be substituted for 2021 shares. Mining variants 1–4 change territorial limits (keep; Bílina; Bílina+partialČSA; both), while perspectives change receptor/value rules within a given variant. No universal one-tonne damage price or current ranking follows. All requested calculations, derivations and qualifications are essential; the component map above applies to every full form.

### O015-D2

O015-D2, item_version 1, full_capability_check. **Prompt:** A hypothetical damage scenario has nonoverlapping additional admission endpoints: Czech receptors 20 cases, other EU receptors 15, and affected non-EU receptors 5; all are in the model’s stated coverage. Uniform EU value is EUR 800/case in a declared common illustrative price year. Relative country-value weights are Czech 0.82, other EU 1.1, non-EU 0.6; these are supplied hypothetical weights, not new empirical country values. Calculate damage under the checked Czech narrow, Czech broad, EU-policy-maker and independent-observer rules. Show the endpoint-unit sum, distinguish receptor boundary from value choice, and explain whether adding a cost-of-illness figure to an already comprehensive WTP value is automatically valid. Interpret why historical 2008 Kč/kWh plant bars, 2021 Danish source shares, 2030 Nordic shares and mining variants 1–4 cannot be collapsed into one current universal damage price.

**Complete solution and essential rubric:** Use $D=\sum_r\Delta I_r v_r$ with cases times EUR/case and one consistent price year. Czech narrow counts only Czech receptors at Czech weights: $20(800)(0.82)=13120.000000$ EUR. Czech broad counts all 40 modelled cases at the same Czech value: $40(800)(0.82)=26240.000000$ EUR. EU-policy-maker coverage in this checked case includes affected non-EU receptors and uses uniform EU values: $40(800)=32000.000000$ EUR. Independent observer counts all modelled receptors with their country-specific weights: $[20(0.82)+15(1.1)+5(0.6)](800)=28720.000000$ EUR. Narrow versus broad changes receptor inclusion with values fixed; broad versus EU changes values with coverage fixed. All-modelled does not mean every global effect is measured, and GDP-based weights are appraisal conventions, not intrinsic human worth. WTP and medical/lost-earnings costs can overlap; add only genuinely separate losses, not automatically a second copy. Historical plant bars are external damages at their configuration/location and stated 2008 price base, not current private tariffs. Danish domestic/foreign source shares concern effects at Danish receptors; deaths abroad are another receptor total. The 2030 Nordic rows have different year/boundary/rounding and cannot be substituted for 2021 shares. Mining variants 1–4 change territorial limits (keep; Bílina; Bílina+partialČSA; both), while perspectives change receptor/value rules within a given variant. No universal one-tonne damage price or current ranking follows. All requested calculations, derivations and qualifications are essential; the component map above applies to every full form.

## Advance, revisit, pause, and escalate

Advance only after teach commits two qualifying independent full passes under a listed route. Keep acquisition and each later delayed observation separate. A source conflict blocks the affected claim and returns to ingest with the exact note heading. Missing criteria, a new method, unsupported alternative or exhausted fresh bank returns to plan with 2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Economics_of_Green_Deal, O015, revision1/O015-C1, P004/V003/ingestion3 and item ID. Equivalent valid methods meeting the frozen criterion may receive credit after verification; no criterion is changed to fit an answer. Closing a session preserves the actual stopping point without claiming completion.

## Content provenance and generation boundaries

Explanations, figures and qualifications above reuse complete checked-note sections with exact origin/fingerprint; heading depth alone is adapted. Main exercises and worked arithmetic are plan-created hypothetical instantiations of those displayed identities. No additional academic claims or external course scope are introduced. Preserve the note conventions and explicit qualifications; checked references reused from notes are not an independent raw-source audit by plan. New numerical practice can use the same method only after its complete solution and unchanged components are checked before display; it cannot replace this lesson’s named evidence forms. Prerequisites route to the complete prepared lessons above.

## Answer-free recall handoff

Topic: Value matched health endpoints under explicit economic standing. Begin a closed-note review with teach for O015; request an unused prepared delayed item before recap. Exact lesson: [[03_Agents/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Economics_of_Green_Deal/lessons/O015.md#Immediate and delayed checks]]. Teach supplies actual committed evidence and timestamps; recall alone dates reviews. No learner outcome or due date is created by this curriculum.
